<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
I/O / INSTRUMENTATION --Allen-Bradlehy 1756-IFxxH
HART Analog Input CHANNEL
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V3.0-00  2013-10-30:   Updated Library of Preferred Integration Objects to V3.0.
Reduced number of MSG control blocks. Adjusted parameter naming.
V3.0-01  2014-01-22:  Backported to V18 of RSLogix 5000.
V3.0-02  2014-04-04: Added checking for and pass thru of
Infinite / NaN values, added parameter descriptions.
V3.1-00  2014-07-09:  Added SrcQ enumerations.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
This Instruction manages a ControlLogixl
Analog Input CHANNEL with HART.
============================================================
Request HART Device Information for Channel 00]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[UIE();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
HART DIGITAL INPUT PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung checks the bit pattern of the REAL input (by copying to a DINT) to see if
the input is +Infinity, -Infinity or Not a Number.  Per ANSI 32-bit Float
format, in these cases the Exponent bits (.30 thru .23) will all be 1s:
0111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = +Infinity
1111 1111 1000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 = -Infinity
x111 1111 1xxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx = Not a Number

#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_PV,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_PVInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_PV,Val_PV,1) CLR(Wrk_SrcQ_PV) ,[XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_PVStatus.7) XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_PVStatus.6) ,XIC(Wrk_PVInfNaN) ] MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ_PV) OTE(Sts_PVBad) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ_PV,SrcQ_PV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_SV,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_SVInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_SV,Val_SV,1) CLR(Wrk_SrcQ_SV) ,[XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_SVStatus.7) XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_SVStatus.6) ,XIC(Wrk_SVInfNaN) ] MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ_SV) OTE(Sts_SVBad) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ_SV,SrcQ_SV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_TV,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_TVInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_TV,Val_TV,1) CLR(Wrk_SrcQ_TV) ,[XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_TVStatus.7) XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_TVStatus.6) ,XIC(Wrk_TVInfNaN) ] MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ_TV) OTE(Sts_TVBad) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ_TV,SrcQ_TV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_FV,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_FVInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[COP(Ref_ChanData.HART_FV,Val_FV,1) CLR(Wrk_SrcQ_FV) ,[XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_FVStatus.7) XIO(Ref_ChanData.HART_FVStatus.6) ,XIC(Wrk_FVInfNaN) ] MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ_FV) OTE(Sts_FVBad) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ_FV,SrcQ_FV) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Ref_ChanData.Data,Wrk_InpDINT,1)MEQ(Wrk_InpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000)OTE(Wrk_AVInfNaN);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.0-02  2014-04-04:  Added checking for Infinite / NaN on all input values;  #####
#####  pass through (avoiding Minor Faults) but flag as BAD.  #####
#####  NOTE:  Sts_PVBad no longer included in Sts_AVBad!!!  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[COP(Ref_ChanData.Data,Val_AV,1) CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIC(Ref_ChanData.Fault) ,XIC(Ref_ChanData.BrokenWire) ,XIC(Wrk_AVInfNaN) ] MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) OTE(Sts_AVBad) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration
#####  V3.1-00  2014-07-09: Added SrcQ enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
HART DIAGNOSTIC MESSAGE
COMMAND 48 CODE
+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Ref_ChanData.HART_FieldDeviceStatus,0)[MOV(0,Val_FaultCode1) ,MOV(0,Val_FaultCode2) ,MOV(0,Val_FaultCode3) ,FLL(0,Wrk_FaultCode[0],3) ,FLL(0,Ref_ChanDiag,1) ,FLL(0,Wrk_N,28) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the HART status is Good from the previous rung, then this logic is skipped skpped to the rung containing the function LBL <EndofLoop>.  200 is moved into Val_ExtSts 1-3. 
If the HART status is not is Good, the HART_DiagData.[0-24 sints] is checked at each bit to see whether or not the bits are true. The first bit of the array is initially checked at sint 0 bit 1 and continues until the first 3 indexed bits [0-199] are collected and put into the prioritized Val_ExtSts 1-3.  

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_DiagT.DN)MOV(5000,Wrk_DiagT.PRE)TON(Wrk_DiagT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Ref_ChanData.HART_FieldDeviceStatus,0)JMP(EndofLoop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_M)CLR(Wrk_N);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Loop0)XIC(Ref_ChanDiag.DiagBit[Wrk_N+16])[MOV(Wrk_N,Wrk_FaultCode[Wrk_M]) ,ADD(Wrk_M,1,Wrk_M) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Wrk_M is less than 3 and Wrk_N is less than 199 than 1 is added to Wrk_N value and the previous rung is executed.  If this rung is false then the next rung is executed.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(Wrk_M,3)LES(Wrk_N,199)[ADD(Wrk_N,1,Wrk_N) ,JMP(Loop0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(EndofLoop)NEQ(Ref_ChanData.HART_FieldDeviceStatus,0)MOV(Wrk_FaultCode[0],Val_FaultCode1)MOV(Wrk_FaultCode[1],Val_FaultCode2)MOV(Wrk_FaultCode[2],Val_FaultCode3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[UID();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="HART_ChanData"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="HART_ChanDiag"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
